		{"id":"e6b80da1d51c4c03","type":"file","file":"PhD-notes/Literature Review/2023 - Business Models for Heat Pumps in Industry 4.0 and digitalisation.md","x":-1418,"y":-718,"width":400,"height":178,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"67cf763c7682bde8","type":"file","file":"PhD-notes/Literature Review/2024 - Research on Strategies for Air-Source Heat Pump Load Aggregation to participate in Multi-Scenario Demand Response.md","x":800,"y":-360,"width":400,"height":186,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"1da15cb43944a89b","type":"text","text":"# Companies that implement HaaS, Operation Optimisation, or Flexible Operations through IoT and digitalisations\n\nFrom the case studies, there are already a lot of companies looking at flexibility and price shifting, and even more that fits into the value chain, performing operation optimisation and preventative maintenance. These are built upon IoT and digitialisation solutions.\n\nThey represent various parts of the value chain, including OEMs, aggregators, service providers, end users. Using this database, we can provide an example of how the value chain can be set up. ~={orange}Map out some interesting examples!=~\n\n![[Screenshot 2026-06-26 175526.png]]\n\nA good question to ask is who should operate the heat pump to maximise the asset lifetime? if there were a centralised access point for electricity market information and heat pump data, then there will be a more thorough and optimised way of efficiently controlling the electrified eco-system.\n- How can we bring these stakeholders together through different interfaces. This can be addressed through standards and regulation development\n### Interesting case studies\n\n| Technology                                                                                     | Use case                                                     | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Links                                                                                                                                                              |     |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --- |\n| Bitzer Heat Pump Ecosystem                                                                     | Heat pump monitoring                                         | Provides an intelligent smart grid read system controller and compressor module. Data can be uploaded to the cloud to eb accessed as backend for commissioning and service tools.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| iDM Energiesysteme                                                                             | Operation Optimisation                                       | Created by HP OEM that makes HP which shifts consumption with heating buffers, hot water storage and thermal building masses. Customer requires an iDM heat pump, smart meter, internet connection and a variable electricity tariff,                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| KNV S Serie                                                                                    | Operation Optimisation                                       | Created by HP OEM that makes HP which shifts consumption based on price and weather forecasts.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| Neusiedl am See districting heating                                                            | Operation Optimisation                                       | Replaced biomass burners with heat pumps and a nearby wind park and battery storage                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| ~={green}Flex+=~                                                                               | ~={green}Flexibility Provision=~                             | ~={green}Explored using heat pumps in providing aFRR and mFRR. Tested on use cases including conventional operation, optimised scheduling based on market price, and reservation of free capacities for frequency restoration reserves. Research project conducted in 2018 for a period of 41 months. It uses flexibility forecast and optimisation of its aggregated pool (from heat pumps to battery storages, to e-boilers, and EVs and smart homes to participate in selling flexibility on Short Term markets. Results showed 65-117 euros of cost reduction for participation on the day-ahead spot market and aFRR participation, and 8-23 euros for only day ahead spot market participation, although this is focused on single family homes. Used MILP for heat pump scheduling.=~                                                  | chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://heatpumpingtechnologies.org/content/uploads/sites/69/2024/12/two-pager-task-2-austria-flex.pdf         |     |\n| ~={green}Energy Demand Control System - EDCSproof=~                                            | ~={green}Operation Optimisation and Flexibility Provision=~  | ~={green}The focus on this study is on optimal process control for SMEs, enabling them to act as flexible consumers and optimise waste heat utilisation. The study looked at i), an operation planner with a prediction horizon, a MPC to follow the trajectory of the op planner iii) an observer to estimate the current state of the system from measurement data. All of this is implemented through a human machine interface.=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| ~={green}ZEB lab heat pump project=~                                                           | ~={green}Operation Optimisation and Predictive maintenance=~ | ~={green}Monitors data from heat pump such as COP and emitted power based on an exergetic approach, This data is executed on actual weather trace to form a benchmark for forecasting. This model is then used to optimise time to transition into night setback mode or operating the heat pump based on PV capacity.=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| ~={green}Swedish project (large scale DR of heat pumps to support the national power system)=~ | ~={green}Flexibility provision=~                             | ~={green}Looked at how aggregation of heat pumps can support a power system through ancillary services, local flexibility markets, or bilateral agreements. The project covers several aspects, such as barriers related to technical constrains in the heat pumps and the electricity market as well as potential communication standards and cybersecurity.=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://etkhpcorderapi.extweb.sp.se/api/file/2609                                                              |     |\n| DIBA-WP                                                                                        | Operation Optimisation                                       | Project to create the foundations of digital operational analysis of HP systems to highlight which settings should be controlled and corrected. Necessary analysis is computationally costly, and so this is where cloud computing come in.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| ~={green}Tiko Energy HP VPP - ENGIE subsidiary=~                                               | ~={green}Flexibility Provision=~                             | ~={green}As of 2017, their virtual power plant already includes 10,000 electrical heating system throughout Switzerland. 1) The K-box measures the power consumption and acts as a control switch 2) The T-box ensures the consumer's comfort level 3) The M-box collects all data and communicates wireless over a 3G-4G network. Their business case revolves around smart metering and innovative IoT solutions, adapting existing heat pumps into internet ready building management solutions. Based on all of this information, they determine the removal or additional of load. They also implement switching limits to prevent heat pumps from over switched. They stopped operating in January, 2025 in France and Switzerland and is currently in commercial liquidation as it was not economically viable to continue operating=~ | chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://heatpumpingtechnologies.org/content/uploads/sites/66/2023/06/iot-annex-56-case-ch-tiko.pdf             |     |\n| SmartGuard system                                                                              | Maintenance and operation optimisation                       | A heat pump manager acts as the controller interface and can redefine various control parameters, to rectify simple settings and faults. In addition, the HP manager collects over 200 data points at 1Hz. An MT-Gateway installs its own antenna on the building facade and communicates via 4G/LTE with the maintenance company's remote diagnostics. In the last category, neogrid provides an aggregator method that blocks and control the heat pumps as a swarm, complying with the constraints of pool operation.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://heatpumpingtechnologies.org/content/uploads/sites/66/2023/04/iot-annex-56-case-dk-neogrid.pdf          |     |\n| Losange project                                                                                | Flexibility provision                                        | Installed heat pumps with hot water tank in two homes in France. Found that they can do short shift load without discomfort for the customer. Required additional equipment to receive signals from the electrical network.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| Digital Twins for large-scale heat pumps                                                       |                                                              | The use of a digital twin allow the service operator to provide monitoring, predictive maintenance, and operation optimisation by comparing plant data with the digital twin. The data is retrieved by wired sensors and IoT based sensors. ~={red}But what is the value of the digital twin when you can just use the data from the sensors?=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| EnergyLab Nordhavn                                                                             | Flexibility Provision and Operational Optimisation           | Used a Danfoss cloud system to retrieve data to a Data Management System (DMS). Connected a supermarket's waste heat to a local district heating facility and determined the optimal operating strategy based on real time operational data and electricity prices. ~={orange}When looking at industry synergies, we can look at the co-location of various assets for waste heat recovery. The program ran from 2015-2019. All activities stopped by 2021=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| ~={green}Flex-heat=~                                                                           | ~={green}Flexibility Provision=~                             | ~={green}Large scale heat pump system that uses a linear optimisation model supported by a dynamic model of the heat pump system to schedule optimal production. This includes heat demand forecast, weather data, stratified storage tank modelling, start-up costs for heat pumps and electricity price forecast to find the minimum cost of heat for the system. Heat pumps have also been modified to provide fast regulation services to the grid. This is just the ammonia cycle heat pump in EnergyLab Nordhavn =~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://heatpumpingtechnologies.org/content/uploads/sites/69/2023/12/dkflexheat2p.pdf                          |     |\n| ~={green}OPSYS 2.0=~                                                                           | ~={green}Flexibility Provision=~                             | ~={green}Increase the efficiency of heat pump installations by developing a control kit that can optimise the forward temperature of the heat pump and the flow rate through heat emitting systems. The control system developed aims to increase.=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | https://www.teknologisk.dk/projekter/projekt-opsys-2-0/40581                                                                                                       |     |\n| SVAF Phase II                                                                                  | Operation Optimisation                                       | Development of HP Autotune and HP Doctor for optimising operating conditions and monitoring faults by adjusting the set points of the heat pump to maximise the COP.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| ~={green}Flexible Energy Denmark=~                                                             | ~={green}Flexibility Provision=~                             | ~={green}Uses Big Data Management to deliver smart grid solutions for heat pumps supplying heat to swimming pools. The control signal is based on grid load forecasts, electricity price, and CO2 forecasts. Showed 15-30% reduction in $CO_2$ emissions where grid services is provided. Also provided balancing services. Project ended in 2023=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| ~={green}DTI - Development of fast regulating heat pumps using dynamic models=~                | ~={green}Flexibility Provision=~                             | ~={green}Improving large scale heat pump technologies to improve ramp times using a digital dynamic model to design advanced control systems. Partners with Johnson's control and is a three year project from 2020 to 2023. The end result is a validation of a screw compressor heat pump dynamics model with a real unit.=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/345457708/8th_international_symposium_Kramer_Meesenburg.pdf |     |\n| Neogrid PreHEAT HP                                                                             | Flexibility Provision and Operation Optimisation             | Sensors record data such as indoor temperature, electricity consumption, and delivered heat are collected and sent to the Neogrid PreHEAT cloud platform. This is then used to prevent overheating or underheating using historical data of the building during weather variations. This data enables 1) MPC control for optimised operations, 2) price shifting and grid services, 3) regulation services, sorted into those numeric categories. However, I cannot find examples of Neogrid providing ancillary services?                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://heatpumpingtechnologies.org/content/uploads/sites/66/2023/04/iot-annex-56-case-dk-neogrid.pdf          |     |\n| ~={green}Centrica Energy Marketing and Trading=~                                               | ~={green}Operation Optimisation and Flexibility Provision=~  | ~={green}Web based API for monitoring heat pumps for district heating. It provides an estimation of the power consumption, heat production, and COP of the heat pump based on outdoor temperature, humidity, wind direction, and wind speed, as well as marginal prices in the electricity market. To date, several Danish district heating companies have adopted the Energy Planning and optimization platform developed by Centrica=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| ~={blue}Narvarmevarket=~                                                                       | ~={blue}Heat as a Service=~                                  | ~={blue}Community owned offering of HaaS . Partners with Vaillandt, Pico, DVI, and HS Tarm to deliver this service (they are all HP suppliers). They implement digital and IoT based solutions that monitor the devices remotely.=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| ~={green}AI-nergy=~                                                                            | ~={green}Flexibility Provision=~                             | ~={green}Uses AI to perform pooling of large scale heat pumps, and optimise scheduling based on forecasted heat demand and prices in the day-ahead and the frequency market. The API also handles the sizing and technology pairing of heat pumps with PV or EV. This example goes to show that there are already value proposition for participation of the heat pump in the frequency market=~                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n| ENFOR                                                                                          | Flexibility Provision and Operation Optimisation             | One of the biggest software provider for wind and solar (25% of the wind market). The temperature control module can be used to improve heat pump efficiency. There is a subsidiary called Heat Solutions that provides this service.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |                                                                                                                                                                    |     |\n\n\nThere are many ways to ","x":140,"y":-290,"width":551,"height":154,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"e8a2bd3a6ba9418c","type":"text","text":"## *Droplet formation in suction pipe during loading change*\n\nDuring the ramp down of the heat pump, the saturation temperature increases above the wall temperature. This causes the condensation of droplets in the compressor and suction line walls. This is due to the increase in evaporation pressure in heat pump.\n- A small increase in evaporation temperature causes a large increase in saturation temperature\n\nThe change with evaporation pressure is due to the power uptake being the proportional to the condensation pressure.\n![[Screenshot 2026-06-15 at 7.02.11 pm.png]]\n\nWe then consult the pressure temperature graph for the refrigerant. \n- Note that at higher pressures, the gradient of the saturation temperature is also lower.\n\nThe constraining of ramping rate of power uptake helps solves the issue\n\nFor other refrigerants, superheating the suction line might actually INCREASE the COP, and therefore not pose a significant issue to heat pump design.","x":173,"y":616,"width":422,"height":91,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"8ac6af62e8602e38","type":"file","file":"PhD-notes/Literature Review/2020 - Heat pumps supplying district heating and ancillary services for power systems - Controls of heat pumps.md","x":218,"y":301,"width":452,"height":159,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"5102b0c404df57a6","type":"text","text":"# ~={orange}EnergyLab Nordhavn=~\n\nhttp://www.energylabnordhavn.com/\n\nInteresting publications that came out of this experiment\n\n- Modelling energy flexibility of low energy buildings utilising thermal mass\n- Intelligent scheduling of grid connected heat pump in a Danish Detached House\n- Performance of ultra low temperature district heating systems with utility plant and booster heat pumps\n- Potential Energy flexibility for a hot water based heating system in smart buildings via economic MPC\n- Quantifying the demand flexibility of power-to-heat and thermal energy storage in the control of building heat systems\n- Demand side management in urban district heating networks\n- Combined provision of primary frequency regulation from V2G EVs and community scale heat pumps","x":340,"y":61,"width":340,"height":132,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c5ed5e8c19d88327","type":"file","file":"PhD-notes/Literature Review/2014 - Aggregation and Control of flexible consumers - A real life demonstration.md","x":800,"y":377,"width":400,"height":178},
		{"id":"cd191c3af19fb78a","type":"file","file":"PhD-notes/Literature Review/2023 - Flexible Energy Denmark.md","x":1260,"y":377,"width":400,"height":89},
		{"id":"fda52721f32fcb2f","type":"file","file":"PhD-notes/Literature Review/2022 - Flex+ demonstration project from AIT.md","x":800,"y":85,"width":400,"height":108,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dc8ec32ab08f4374","type":"text","text":"# Tiko Energy Solutions -when financing risk outweighs market revenue\n\nhttps://kurrant.com/kurrantly-news/engie-subsidiary-tiko-shuts-down-in-france-leaving-thousands-without-smart-heating-controls/\n\nDemand response is necessary, IEA forecast that 500GW of demand response is needed globally by 2030, requiring an investment of 2030. \n\nTiko energy solution was a built on government subsidies. Originally founded in 2012 as Swisscom Energy Solutions, was acquired by Engie in March 2019.\n\nFlexibility was sold to RTE, the French transmission operator. Revenue flowed from France's Energy Savings Certificates and from the government's Coup de Pouce Pilotage connecte du chauffage piece par piece bonus scheme.\n- This bonus scheme was terminated in November 2024, after the Ministry of Energy Transition detected widespread fraud across the broader thermostate subsidy sector.\n- Within weeks, tiko liquidated\n\nIssue further compounded when internal quality assessment identified overheating risks that could cause fires. Items were recalled without replacement since the manufacturer had already shut down.\n- But this was in December 2025, long after tiko had liquidated\n\nConsumers are left with thermostats and contorl devices that are unable to connect to third party systems. \n- There are also regulatory pressure for smart metering, with deadlines by January 2030 for all homes to convert.\n- Consumers are starting to convert to Voltais, which has 250,000 equipped buildings and 1.5 million connected appliance across $8$ European countries. They signed a 721 MW, 10 year demand response contract. In 2024, Voltais secured 215 million euros to rollout 1.4GWp of demand response.\n\nThey collaborated with EVN in Austria to propose Joulie is an intelligent assisstant that continuously learns your consumption habits so that electricity sonumption is optimised and revenue is optimised. It comes with a PV system that is managed along with a battery. Joulie can be monitored through an online interface.\n\nThe energy assistant was developed in collaboration with tiko to decentralise energy supplies. Taking advantage of the flexibility of heat pumps and EVs to perform grid services whilst sharing that benefit with consumers.\n","x":-309,"y":118,"width":329,"height":162,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ff0d9bea75f1d19e","type":"text","text":"# Voltalis - Largest European Demand Response Aggregator","x":-351,"y":338,"width":371,"height":122},
